2026-10-16T14:57:51.6905714Z   ISSUE_TITLE: Subagent runs fail with 'model_coming_soon' on MiMo-V2.6-Flash while the main session on the same model works fine
2026-10-16T14:57:51.6908185Z   ISSUE_BODY: ### Description

Every subagent launch started failing ~5 minutes ago (22:45-22:50 +08:00, 2026-10-16), after everything worked fine for hours. The main session on **MiMo-V2.6-Flash** keeps working with zero errors (already at ~240k token context), but every subagent run on the same model gets rejected:

\\\
Subagent failed (task_id: ...): Upstream request failed: [model_coming_soon] This model is coming soon.
\\\

Subagents start from a fresh context (near-zero tokens), so the failing call is the CHEAPER one, while the big-context main-thread call succeeds. Tried 4 launches in a row, all failed: subagent_type=explore x3, subagent_type=general x1. Same model, same provider config, main thread fine / subagent dead. Nothing changed config-wise — it just started ~5 min ago after hours of working (6 subagent runs succeeded earlier tonight on the same model).

### Plugins

(none)

### OpenCode version

1.18.32

### Steps to reproduce

1. Hours of normal use with subagents working fine (6 subagent runs succeeded earlier tonight on MiMo-V2.6-Flash)
2. ~22:45 +08:00 the same subagent launches start failing instantly
3. Launch any subagent (explore or general) -> \Upstream request failed: [model_coming_soon]\
4. Main session on the exact same model keeps responding normally

### Screenshot and/or share link

n/a

